[PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]
## Consolidated Experience from Similar Tasks
To move an object to a target, first locate the source object; do not assume it is directly visible or findable. If the initial find fails, inspect likely containers or occluding receptacles and retry or explore alternatives. Before attempting pick_up, navigate to the object and ensure it is within reach; pick_up only succeeds when proximity preconditions are met. After pick_up, verify that the object is actually being held. To place the object, locate the target surface or receptacle; if the named target instance is unavailable, explore other instances or retry rather than stopping. Before executing put_down, verify that the robot is holding the object and perform pick_up first if needed. Success requires a successful find and pick_up of the object, a successful find of the target location, and a final successful put_down.

## Preliminary Thinking
1. Locate the spoon on the right counter. If it is not directly visible, inspect likely containers or occluding receptacles near the right counter, then retry. 2. Navigate to the spoon, verify it is within reach, and execute pick_up. Confirm the spoon is held. 3. Locate the left counter and its right receptacle. If the right receptacle is not directly found, explore or retry other instances on the left counter rather than stopping. 4. Navigate to the right receptacle while holding the spoon. 5. Execute put_down to place the spoon into the right receptacle and verify success.
[/PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]